      },
      "lineNbr": 137,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004017
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-02-06T03:19:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Clients? Are you referring to gid?  This is a reference to the same gid as passed to the enroll function. We currently only support one group, but this is a parallel API to the fingerprint one, so I suggest keeping it.\n\nThe id refers to the exact iris id known to the framework. There\u0027s exactly one, so it doesn\u0027t necessarily need to be listed here, but it doesn\u0027t hurt.  Passing 0, means everything.\n\nFrom a process-perspective, there\u0027s only one client, IrisManager.  It must arbitrate all access to this HAL, like we do in fingerprint.",
      "parentUuid": "ab36774f_d58ba603",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 137,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 137,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "254eb0a54f006df271f3e9c06c434d31549a096a",
